<title>JORDAN: Aqaba port discharges 6,496 T of Iraq-bound rice.</title>
<headline>Aqaba port discharges 6,496 T of Iraq-bound rice.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A vessel carrying 6,496 tonnes of Thai rice has discharged on Thursday its Iraq-bound cargo at Jordan's Red Sea port of Aqaba, Jordanian traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said the Bahamas-flagged vessel Diamond Ray which had been in Aqaba since Sunday had now offloaded the rice consigment bought by Iraq's state gains purchasing body.</p>
<p>Iraq's monthly consumption of rice is around 25,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Amman Newsroom +9626-623776</p>
